# ## 8. Data Sources, Provenance, and Usage Records
# 
# ### 8.1 Purpose of Our Source Register
# 
# We will document where our datasets and references came from, which versions we intend to use, how prepared files relate to their inputs, and which source questions remain open. This register will support the data-loading, quality-review, and catalog steps that follow.
# 
# Our records will distinguish original publisher material, prepared datasets, fictional profiles, derived retrieval documents, and audit reports. A prepared table and its retrieval representation will remain linked to the same underlying evidence rather than count as independent sources.
# 
# We will maintain `data/source_manifest.csv` as our curated source register. A separate file inventory will record what we can inspect locally during each run. Keeping these records separate will let us compare current files with their recorded versions while preserving source documentation and review decisions.
# 
# ### 8.2 Source Families and Their Roles
# 
# | Source family | Role in our project | Main provenance questions |
# |---|---|---|
# | Gym exercise records | Body-part classification and exercise catalog preparation | Original release, labels, source identifiers, and usage terms |
# | Jr. NBA/Jr. WNBA curriculum | Basketball coaching evidence and drill candidates | Practice-plan locations, source occurrences, summaries, adaptations, and reuse terms |
# | NBA/USA Basketball guidance | Participation and scheduling references | Applicable age or grade group, rule interpretation, and source version |
# | FoodData Central Foundation Foods | General food and nutrient reference | Acquired archive, food identifiers, units, energy methods, and preparation history |
# | FoodData Central SR Legacy | Planned alternative food reference | April 2018 release and any future acquisition, kept distinct from Foundation Foods |
# | CDC and American Academy of Pediatrics references | Sleep and recovery background | Source documents, applicability, and the distinction between published guidance and our interpretation |
# | Fictional athlete profiles | Development scenarios and later benchmark preparation | Generator history, identifiers, related variations, and evaluation partitions |
# | Historical basketball statistics | Optional contextual analysis | Publisher, release, relevance, and permitted use |
# 
# The original cleaned package also contains food linkage tables, athlete examples, a combined master file, and a cleaning audit. We will inspect these as prepared inputs while retaining their unresolved original-source questions.
# 
# The master file is a heterogeneous record index. Task-specific tables will supply classifier inputs and reference preparation. We will establish explicit identifiers and documented relationships before joining data across domains.
# 
# ### 8.3 Prepared Inputs and Execution Order
# 
# Our available preparation work includes structured basketball occurrences and derived RAG documents, a Foundation Foods table and quality report, fictional profiles, recovery guidance, and a versioned youth basketball rule register.
# 
# We will preserve their existing source identifiers and preparation references. Earlier identifiers will remain stable even when we improve the surrounding documentation. Recorded commits will describe preparation history; they will not establish an external publication date or independently authenticate a local file.
# 
# Step 8 will require the original prepared package and the integrated preparation inputs. Catalog outputs produced later will be optional at this checkpoint:
# 
# | Registered output | Producing step |
# |---|---|
# | Exercise catalog | Steps 10–11 |
# | Initial basketball catalog and working table | Step 12 |
# | Expanded basketball review catalog | Step 12 |
# 
# If these later files already exist, we will inspect their saved copies. If they have not been produced, we will record that status and continue. Subsequent catalog versions and their evidence packages will be registered as their producing steps establish them. The number of source records can therefore grow with the project.
# 
# ### 8.4 File Integrity and Lineage Checks
# 
# For locally available files, we will measure size, SHA-256 checksum, and record count where applicable. Counts from the earlier cleaning audit will remain distinguishable from our independent file counts.
# 
# We will check that source and issue identifiers are nonempty and unique, parent references resolve, the source graph has no cycles, and declared file paths remain inside our project. Missing historical inputs will retain their expected locations instead of disappearing from the register.
# 
# We will also check identifier correspondence between structured drills and derived RAG documents, the identifiers and fictional-data markers in the profile examples, and recovery-rule identifiers. The versioned recovery v0.1 file will retain its recorded checksum check.
# 
# These checks establish file integrity and documented relationships. They do not verify every coaching instruction, activate participation rules, or establish data suitability. Detailed nutrition screening and other quality analysis will take place in Step 9.
# 
# ### 8.5 Review Decisions and Usage Terms
# 
# We will preserve existing source descriptions, dates, permissions, limitations, issue statuses, and additional documentation columns. Current file measurements will be written to the audit reports rather than silently replacing recorded hashes or source-verification dates.
# 
# A changed required input will require review of its version and lineage before the register is updated. Changes to saved later outputs will be reported for reconciliation in their producing steps. Existing artifact-bound decisions will require review whenever their underlying contents change.
# 
# FoodData Central documents CC0 terms for its data. We will retain that source-policy information while separately checking whether our prepared files are traceable to the stated USDA release. We will keep the older food tables' unresolved provenance separate from this policy.
# 
# For exercise data, coaching content, and other references, we will document the applicable terms for storage, transformation, model use, retrieval, display, and redistribution. Attribution and permission will remain separate records. This audit will preserve pending decisions and will not assign catalog approval or planner eligibility.
# 
# ### 8.6 Outputs and Handoff
# 
# We will use three code cells to define the source records, inspect files and relationships, and save the results.
# 
# | Output | Purpose |
# |---|---|
# | `data/source_manifest.csv` | Curated source records and declared lineage |
# | `results/provenance_followups.csv` | Open and completed provenance work, with existing statuses preserved |
# | `results/source_file_inventory.csv` | Current paths, hashes, counts, availability, and comparisons with recorded facts |
# | `results/source_lineage_checks.csv` | Required and informational check results |
# | `results/source_manifest_changes.csv` | Proposed and applied source-register changes |
# | `results/step08_source_audit_summary.json` | Audit scope, counts, issue statuses, and final outcome |
# 
# We will validate the records before updating the source and issue ledgers. Changed documentation will be backed up, and a failed output update will trigger restoration of the files already written. If required source checks fail, we will save diagnostic reports while leaving those two ledgers unchanged.
# 
# The code will inspect local files without refreshing publisher pages or downloading new datasets. A local audit timestamp will remain separate from acquisition dates and recorded source-verification dates.
# 
# Step 9 will use this register and its current inventory to load the relevant datasets and review their quality. We will finalize this step's observations after inspecting the execution output.
# 
# ### 8.7 Source References
# 
# - [Gym Exercise Dataset](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/niharika41298/gym-exercise-data)
# - [Jr. NBA/Jr. WNBA curriculum](https://jr.nba.com/jr-nba-instructional-curriculum/)
# - [NBA/USA Basketball youth guidelines](https://youthguidelines.nba.com/)
# - [FoodData Central downloads and releases](https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/download-datasets/)
# - [FoodData Central usage terms](https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-guide/#licensing)
# - [CDC sleep background](https://www.cdc.gov/sleep/about/)
# - [AAP report on overuse, overtraining, and burnout](https://doi.org/10.1542/peds.2023-065129)
# 
# ---
# 

