# ### Step 14 — Observations
# 
# We completed the USDA food-reference data-preparation checkpoint and saved a frozen prototype snapshot for Step 24. The snapshot contains 100 selected SR Legacy foods with source-linked nutrient and portion records. Preparation and calculation checks passed; the application's food lookup remains disabled until Step 24 integration.
# 
# #### Source identity and preservation of earlier work
# 
# We first verified the existing 411-row Foundation Foods reference against the saved Step 11 findings. Its screening results remained unchanged: 321 foods had finite values for the four core fields, while 313 had finite nonnegative values for all four. Eight records contained a negative carbohydrate value. Fiber was missing for 204 foods, and selected energy was missing for 89. These remain findings about the earlier Foundation table; we did not transfer them to SR Legacy, correct its values, or relabel its data type.
# 
# The local inventory found no USDA raw archives or tables in the searched project locations. We therefore acquired the official SR Legacy CSV package listed by USDA as the April 2018 release. The downloaded archive contained 6,074,592 bytes and had SHA-256:
# 
# `b80817294b8850530aaedf2e515c02593b1824f763a0ff356e5c2081643e6fd0`
# 
# We saved the source URL, catalog snapshot, acquisition time, HTTP metadata, archive, extracted-table hashes, and producer record. The acquired package included the required supporting definitions, so no separate supporting archive was used. Its 17 CSV tables included food identities, nutrient values, nutrient definitions, categories, measures, portions, and derivation information.
# 
# All 7,793 food records were labelled `sr_legacy_food`. Their FoodData Central publication date was `2019-04-01`; we retained this separately from the underlying April 2018 release and our download time.
# 
# #### Full-source validation findings
# 
# The acquired source contained 7,793 foods, 644,125 food–nutrient rows, and 474 nutrient definitions. All 644,125 nutrient rows joined successfully to food identities and nutrient definitions, with no duplicate food–nutrient pairs. The source-validation stage passed 48 checks, matched the reviewed USDA documentation snapshots, and saved nine evidence tables, four JSON documents, two reference PDFs, and a producer record.
# 
# We confirmed the documented per-100-gram edible-food basis and preserved units from the nutrient dictionary. For the selected display concepts, we used exact nutrient identifiers: energy `1008`, protein `1003`, total fat `1004`, carbohydrate by difference `1005`, and dietary fiber `1079`. Energy `1008` was recorded in `KCAL`. The acquired SR nutrient-value table contained no records for Foundation energy identifiers `2047` or `2048`; we did not substitute those fields or recalculate energy from a general macronutrient formula.
# 
# All 7,793 source foods had finite nonnegative recorded values for the four core display nutrients. Fiber records were absent for 562 foods. We treated absence as unavailable rather than zero.
# 
