# ### Observations — Step 19: Majority-Class and TF-IDF Logistic Regression Baselines
# 
# We completed the initial baseline comparison and saved both fitted models with their validation evidence. These are development results; model selection and final held-out evaluation remain later steps.
# 
# #### 1. Shared Benchmark and Validation Results
# 
# Both baselines used the same 1,999 training records from 1,794 groups and the same 435 validation records from 384 groups. Scoring retained the complete frozen order of 16 benchmark classes, with macro-F1 as the primary measure and `zero_division=0`.
# 
# | Model | Correct validation records | Validation accuracy | Validation macro-F1 |
# |---|---:|---:|---:|
# | Majority class | 83 / 435 | 0.190805 | 0.020029 |
# | TF-IDF logistic regression | 308 / 435 | 0.708046 | 0.470967 |
# 
# Logistic regression improved validation accuracy by 51.724138 percentage points and macro-F1 by approximately 0.450938. Full-precision values remain in the saved results; the table is rounded for display.
# 
# The majority model selected `abdominals`, frozen class index 0, from its training support of 473 out of 1,999 records (23.661831%). No training-count tie occurred. Its choice came from training labels, while validation labels were used for scoring.
# 
# #### 2. Initial Logistic Regression and Feature Preparation
# 
# The learned baseline used L2 regularization, `C=1.0`, the `lbfgs` solver, no class or sample weighting, and tolerance `1e-4`. It completed its first 1,000-iteration-limit attempt in 45 solver iterations, with zero recorded fit warnings. The recorded fit-call duration was 0.668008 seconds; this is not whole-workflow runtime. The predefined 5,000-iteration retry was not needed.
# 
# The pipeline accepts canonical `classifier_text` and applies the shared normalization/tokenizer exactly once per pass. TF-IDF uses word unigrams and bigrams, sparse float64 features and L2 row normalization. Its vocabulary and IDF values were fitted on training text only and remained unchanged during validation.
# 
# | Split | Records | Feature columns | Nonzero values | Zero-vector records |
# |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
# | Training | 1,999 | 10,000 | 91,261 | 10 |
# | Validation | 435 | 10,000 | 17,649 | 2 |
# 
# Both zero-vector validation inputs received the pipeline’s ordinary predictions and stayed in the 435-record denominator. Neither was correct. Neural vocabulary limits and sequence truncation were not applied to TF-IDF.
# 
# #### 3. Per-Class and Input Diagnostics
# 
# The per-class report shows limitations that overall accuracy alone does not describe. Abductors, adductors and traps received no predictions, despite validation supports of three, three and four records respectively. Their recall and F1 were zero. Undefined precision is separately flagged under the saved scoring convention.
# 
# For logistic regression, the text-availability breakdown was:
# 
# | Validation input | Records | Correct | Accuracy | Macro-F1 |
# |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
# | Name only | 234 | 155 | 0.662393 | 0.460710 |
# | Name and description | 201 | 153 | 0.761194 | 0.467824 |
# 
# These are descriptive subsets. They do not establish that adding a description causes better predictions, because the records and class composition differ. Distinct exercise groups can occur in more than one subset, so subgroup group counts must not be summed as independent groups. Each subset report retains all 16 classes in its macro-F1 calculation; the headline comparison remains the complete validation partition.
# 
# The largest recorded logistic-regression confusion pairs included quadriceps → abdominals (14 records), lats → middle back (nine), and hamstrings → quadriceps (eight).
# 
# The error audit contains 479 model/record rows: 352 majority-model errors and 127 logistic-regression errors. These are not 479 distinct exercises. The audit links disagreements to exercise text and group identifiers for review. Human source-label review remains pending, and no benchmark labels were changed automatically.
# 
# #### 4. Saved Artifacts and Reload Verification
