# ### Observations — Step 21: Validation, Hyperparameter Tuning, and Model Selection
# 
# We completed the predefined classifier search and froze the selected research artifacts and tagging decision. L5 was selected for logistic regression and application tagging. N3 was selected as the neural configuration, with its seed-42, epoch-19 checkpoint retained for the final classifier comparison. These are development selections; final held-out evaluation remains Step 32.
# 
# #### 1. Fixed Benchmark and Search Budget
# 
# All candidates used the same 1,999 training records from 1,794 groups and 435 validation records from 384 groups. Scoring retained all 16 frozen classes, used `zero_division=0`, and selected models using unrounded validation macro-F1. Accuracy and diagnostic subsets did not replace that measure.
# 
# The versioned search plan fixed six logistic configurations and eight neural configuration/seed combinations. L2 from Step 19 and N0 with seed 42 from Step 20 were verified and reused. The remaining work comprised five new logistic fitting attempts and seven new neural training runs. No logistic convergence retry was needed, and all scheduled outcomes were completed or verified reuses, with no recorded warnings or failed runs.
# 
# Text preparation, TF-IDF settings, the neural architecture, training-derived vocabulary and sequence limit, split membership and target mapping remained fixed. Class weights were calculated from training targets only. No candidate was fitted on combined training and validation data.
# 
# #### 2. Logistic Regression Selection
# 
# | Candidate | C | Class weighting | Validation accuracy | Validation macro-F1 |
# |---|---:|---|---:|---:|
# | L0 | 0.1 | None | 0.468966 | 0.146453 |
# | L1 | 0.1 | Balanced | 0.627586 | 0.527872 |
# | L2, verified Step 19 reference | 1.0 | None | 0.708046 | 0.470967 |
# | L3 | 1.0 | Balanced | 0.703448 | 0.573719 |
# | L4 | 10.0 | None | 0.728736 | 0.557628 |
# | L5, selected | 10.0 | Balanced | 0.724138 | 0.598009 |
# 
# L5 had the highest validation macro-F1. L4 had the highest accuracy, but the saved selection rule favored macro-F1 and therefore retained L5. At each tested C value, the balanced version had higher macro-F1 than its unweighted counterpart.
# 
# Relative to the initial L2 baseline, L5 improved macro-F1 by approximately 0.127042 and accuracy by 1.609195 percentage points. This was seven additional correct validation predictions. These differences describe this fixed development partition and do not establish a statistically reliable advantage.
# 
# #### 3. Neural Configuration and Checkpoint Selection
# 
# The seed-42 comparison evaluated three individual changes relative to N0.
# 
# | Candidate | Learning rate | Dropout | Loss weighting | Validation accuracy | Validation macro-F1 |
# |---|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|
# | N0, verified Step 20 reference | 0.001 | 0.2 | None | 0.724138 | 0.540130 |
# | N1 | 0.0003 | 0.2 | None | 0.664368 | 0.359741 |
# | N2 | 0.001 | 0.4 | None | 0.724138 | 0.527938 |
# | N3 | 0.001 | 0.2 | Training-frequency weights | 0.682759 | 0.571145 |
# 
# N3 and N0 formed the frozen shortlist. N1 and N2 did not improve seed-42 macro-F1 within the planned training budget. This limited search does not establish that their settings could never work better under another documented experiment.
# 
# Each shortlisted configuration was repeated at seeds 17 and 73, with fresh weights, optimizer state and separate shuffle generators. The complete three-seed comparison was:
# 
# | Configuration | Seed 42 macro-F1 | Seed 17 macro-F1 | Seed 73 macro-F1 | Mean macro-F1 | Sample standard deviation |
# |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
# | N3, selected | 0.571145 | 0.553626 | 0.562598 | 0.562456 | 0.008760 |
# | N0 | 0.540130 | 0.555869 | 0.510216 | 0.535405 | 0.023190 |
# 
# N3's mean exceeded N0's by approximately 0.027051. N3 also showed less variation across these three runs. The sample standard deviations use `ddof=1`; they describe training variation on this split and are not confidence intervals or uncertainty across independent athlete populations.
# 
# The predefined rule retained N3's best seed-42 checkpoint, selected at epoch 19. That run completed 24 epochs before exhausting patience. Configuration selection used all three seed scores; checkpoint selection retained seed 42 as specified in advance. No alternative seed or ensemble was substituted.
# 
# N3 used training-frequency-weighted cross-entropy, while N0 used unweighted cross-entropy. Their loss values describe different objectives and were not used to rank configurations. Validation macro-F1 remained ordinary record-based scoring across all 16 classes.
# 
# #### 4. Frozen Comparison Artifacts and Tagging Decision
# 
# | Frozen artifact | Correct validation records | Validation accuracy | Validation macro-F1 |
# |---|---:|---:|---:|
# | Majority-class baseline | 83 / 435 | 0.190805 | 0.020029 |
# | Logistic regression L5 | 315 / 435 | 0.724138 | 0.598009 |
# | Neural N3, seed 42, epoch 19 | 297 / 435 | 0.682759 | 0.571145 |
# 
# The tagging decision compared the scores of the actual L5 pipeline and N3 seed-42 checkpoint. N3's three-seed mean selected its configuration; it was not used as the tagging artifact score.
# 
# L5 exceeded N3's primary artifact by approximately 0.026864 macro-F1 and 4.137931 accuracy percentage points, corresponding to 18 additional correct records. L5 also strictly exceeded the majority baseline, satisfying the predefined tagging gate. Its selected settings are `C=10.0` with balanced class weights.
# 
# Selecting L5 identifies the classifier to package in Step 22. Its predictions remain category suggestions under review; selection does not approve an exercise or make a basketball drill eligible for planning. Existing catalog labels and their review status were not changed.
# 
# #### 5. Input Diagnostics and Interpretation Limits
# 
# | Selected model | Validation input | Records | Correct | Accuracy | Macro-F1 |
# |---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
# | L5 | Name only | 234 | 164 | 0.700855 | 0.596602 |
# | L5 | Name and description | 201 | 151 | 0.751244 | 0.575881 |
# | N3, seed 42 | Name only | 234 | 152 | 0.649573 | 0.564078 |
# | N3, seed 42 | Name and description | 201 | 145 | 0.721393 | 0.583413 |
# 
# Both models had higher accuracy on records containing descriptions. L5's macro-F1, however, was lower in that subset than on name-only records. These subsets contain different records and class compositions, so the results do not isolate a causal benefit from adding descriptions. Subsets can share groups, and their group counts should not be summed as independent groups. All subset macro-F1 calculations retain the complete 16-class denominator.
# 
# The saved diagnostics include per-class reports, confusion counts and row proportions, truncation and unknown-token subsets, TF-IDF zero-vector cases, and the primary neural run's learning history. Undefined precision retains its definition flag, and empty subsets retain unavailable scores. Missing epoch fields for logistic regression and missing neural seed statistics for non-neural artifacts are inapplicable fields, not failed experiments.
# 
# TF-IDF uses full prepared text, while the neural model uses the saved sequence limit of 81 tokens. This representation difference remains part of the comparison. Model probability outputs remain uncalibrated. Human source-label review is still pending, and prediction disagreements do not by themselves show that the source labels are wrong.
# 
# #### 6. Verification, Saved Evidence and Handoff
# 
# The final selection stage reverified 250 prior input and search files and saved 289 selection checks, including 13 checks from 13 artificial final-selection scenarios. These are implementation and integrity checks, not additional model experiments.
# 
# Fresh Python processes replayed the three original references and reloaded the two selected learned artifacts. The consolidated selected-artifact predictions contain 1,305 rows: three models evaluated on the same 435 validation records, rather than 1,305 distinct exercises. The frozen 16-column probability order and recorded outputs were verified.
# 
# Step 21-5 created 16 final-stage files, including the model-selection record, complete candidate and validation tables, selected predictions and per-class reports, diagnostic tables, three figures, a plain-language summary and the producer record. Earlier search plans, model files, shortlist and seed summaries remained unchanged. The selected models retain their original training-partition fits; the freeze cell performed no additional fitting or training.
# 
# Step 21 classifier search and model selection are complete. Repeated validation use for checkpointing and tuning makes these results development evidence. No held-out test text was transformed, predicted or scored, and final test results will not silently switch the frozen classifier supplied to later workflows.
# 
# Step 22 will package the explicitly identified artifacts and define reviewed tagging use. Step 32 remains responsible for final held-out classifier evaluation. Planner acceptance, human label review and full operational evaluation readiness remain pending independently.
# 

# <hr style="border: none; height: 10px; background-color: #FFD700;">

# ## 22. Saving the Classifier and Tagging the Catalog
# 
# ### 22.1 Purpose
# 
# We will package the selected classifiers so our teammates and application can load them without repeating training.
# 
# We will also prepare a controlled workflow for suggesting body-part tags for compatible new or unlabeled exercise records.
# 
# Three decisions will remain separate:
# 
# - Whether the saved model bundle loads and works correctly.
# - Whether a suggested body-part tag has been accepted through review.
# - Whether an exercise is eligible for use in a youth training plan.
# 
# A successful model-loading check will establish the first of these. It will not automatically establish the others.
# 
# ### 22.2 Verify and Preserve the Selected Models
# 
# We will begin with the model-selection record and producer summary from Step 21.
# 
# The research bundle will preserve all three comparison artifacts.
# 
# | Model | Artifact to preserve |
# |---|---|
# | Majority-class baseline | The fitted model with its training-derived constant prediction |
# | Logistic regression | The selected complete normalization, TF-IDF, and classifier pipeline |
# | Neural classifier | The selected configuration’s best seed-42 checkpoint |
# 
# We will verify the model identifiers, input hashes, class mapping, preprocessing versions, and validation results against the selection record.
# 
# Packaging will preserve the actual selected artifacts. It will not refit a model, change the neural seed, combine checkpoints, or rebuild a vocabulary.
# 
# The tagging-model decision will also come directly from Step 21. If tagging was disabled, packaging the research models can still succeed.
# 
# If model selection remains incomplete, we may prepare a provisional bundle, but we will record that status rather than declare a verified release.
# 
# ### 22.3 Package the Models and Their Dependencies
# 
# Each release will have a versioned folder under:
# 
# `artifacts/classifiers/<release_id>/`
# 
# The bundle will contain the fitted models together with the information needed to interpret their inputs and outputs.
# 
# | Bundle component | Purpose |
# |---|---|
# | Fitted majority model | Reproduce the baseline prediction |
# | Complete logistic regression pipeline | Preserve normalization, tokenization, vocabulary, IDF values, and classifier parameters |
# | Neural state dictionary | Restore the selected learned weights |
# | Neural architecture configuration | Reconstruct the correct network dimensions |
# | Preprocessing configuration | Reproduce the Step 18 text rules |
# | Neural vocabulary | Preserve token-to-ID assignments |
# | Sequence and masking settings | Reproduce truncation, padding, and pooling |
# | Label mapping | Decode class indices correctly |
# | Dependency information | Recreate the recorded model environment |
# | Required project source modules | Load custom functions and network definitions outside the notebook |
# 
# The reusable implementation will remain under `src/champion_athletic_map/`. The release will include a versioned copy of the required source package with its import paths preserved.
# 
# We will record both the Git revision, where available, and the hashes of the actual source files. This will also account for relevant changes that have not yet been committed.
# 
# For scikit-learn models, we will use `joblib` with the recorded dependency versions.
# 
# For the neural model, we will save its `state_dict` and reconstruct the network from the saved configuration. Loading will use an explicit device mapping, `weights_only=True` where supported, and strict parameter matching.
# 
# These artifacts will support inference and evaluation. They will not be described as complete checkpoints for resuming the exact training process.
# 
# ### 22.4 Create a Versioned Manifest
# 
# The bundle’s `manifest.json` will identify:
# 
# - Release and model IDs.
# - The three research artifacts.
# - The selected tagging model, or its disabled or pending status.
# - The Step 21 selection record and decision reason.
# - Dataset and split versions.
# - Preprocessing, vocabulary, sequence, and label-map versions.
# - Neural configuration, seed, and selected epoch.
# - Validation scores used for selection.
# - Source-code revision and file hashes.
# - Python and relevant package versions.
# - Training, reference-inference, and intended application devices.
# - Bundle filenames and their hashes.
# - Supported classes, input requirements, and known limitations.
# 
# Paths inside the bundle will be relative to its release directory so the package can be moved without depending on one teammate’s folder structure.
# 
# The manifest will contain hashes for its payload files. The external Step 22 producer record will hash the completed manifest and verification reports.
# 
# We will preserve earlier releases. A repeated run may reuse an identical verified bundle, but it will not silently overwrite a different release.
# 
# The application will load the explicit model ID in the manifest rather than assume that the newest model file is the selected one.
# 
# ### 22.5 Provide a Common Prediction Interface
# 
# We will create a reusable interface that accepts an exercise name and an optional description.
# 
# It will:
# 
# 1. Validate the supplied fields.
# 2. Construct the same name-first canonical text used in Step 10, with two newline characters between nonempty name and description fields.
# 3. Apply the saved Step 18 preparation exactly once.
# 4. Run the explicitly selected model.
# 5. Decode the result with the frozen class mapping.
# 6. Return the prediction, model version, and relevant handling flags.
# 
# For logistic regression, canonical text will go directly into the complete saved pipeline. The neural interface will apply its saved normalization and token preparation. Each route will apply its preparation exactly once.
# 
# A missing description will be allowed. A missing or invalid exercise name will return an explained input error.
# 
# Identifiers, labels, and review metadata will remain outside the model features.
# 
# The response will distinguish a produced prediction from disabled tagging, invalid input, unsupported records, deferred records, or a loading error.
# 
# Depending on the model, handling flags may include name-only input, truncation, unknown-token coverage, or an all-zero TF-IDF vector.
# 
# If scores are returned, the response will identify their type and class order. Probabilities will remain uncalibrated model outputs rather than verified confidence.
# 
# Missing files, incompatible mappings, or failed integrity checks will return a clear error. They will not trigger an undocumented replacement model or majority-class fallback.
# 
# ### 22.6 Verify Loading in a Fresh Process
# 
# We will test loading in a fresh Python process using the recorded dependencies and bundled project modules.
# 
# This process must work without relying on fitted objects or function definitions held in notebook memory.
# 
# We will compare predictions for the complete saved validation partition with the selected artifacts’ reference predictions.
# 
# The checks will confirm that:
# 
# - Required files and source modules are available.
# - File hashes match the manifest.
# - Canonical input construction and normalized text match the saved development inputs.
# - Vocabulary, sequence settings, and class ordering are correct.
# - Decoded predictions match the recorded results.
# - Numerical outputs remain finite and agree within the predefined tolerance.
# - Prediction does not alter learned parameters or preprocessing artifacts.
# - Neural inference uses evaluation mode with gradients disabled.
# 
# Our initial numerical comparison tolerance will be `rtol=1e-5` and `atol=1e-6`. Predicted labels must match exactly in the recorded reference environment.
# 
# We will also check the intended application device. A label difference will require investigation even when the underlying scores are numerically close.
# 
# Separate fixed synthetic fixtures will check missing descriptions, extra whitespace, long text, unknown tokens, and padding behavior. These fixtures will test input handling, rather than provide additional classification-accuracy evidence.
# 
# No held-out test examples will be used for these checks.
# 
# ### 22.7 Define the Tagging Population
# 
# When Step 21 has selected an available tagging model, the initial workflow will cover:
# 
# - Eligible training and validation records used for development previews.
# - Compatible new general-exercise records needing a body-part suggestion.
# 
# Existing source labels will be preserved. We will not bulk-replace them with model predictions.
# 
# Training previews will be marked as in-sample outputs. Validation previews will be marked as development outputs. Neither will become additional evidence of generalization.
# 
# Held-out test records and their groups will remain outside the tagging pass until the final classifier evaluation.
# 
# New records will be screened using the existing conservative grouping policy. Records that match, or may belong to, a protected test group will be deferred. This screening will not change the frozen benchmark or its split assignments.
# 
# Known unsupported record types and categories outside the classifier’s demonstrated scope will also be deferred or skipped with an explanation.
# 
# The development catalog export will contain only the defined development tagging population. A separate population report will account for processed, skipped, deferred, disabled, and failed records.
# 
# If tagging is disabled, the prediction export may contain no new suggestions. We will report that outcome directly rather than generate replacement predictions from another model.
# 
# ### 22.8 Preserve Label Origins and Review Decisions
# 
# The derived catalog will retain existing source values and distinguish them from review decisions and predictions.
# 
# | Field | Meaning |
# |---|---|
# | `source_body_part` | The prepared source-provided label, linked to its original wording |
# | `source_verification_status` | The recorded verification status of that source label |
# | `reviewed_body_part` | A label adopted through an identifiable review decision |
# | `predicted_body_part` | The classifier’s suggested label |
# | `prediction_model_version` | The release that produced the suggestion |
# | `prediction_input_hash` | The exact input version used for prediction |
# | `prediction_status` | Whether prediction was produced, skipped, deferred, disabled, or failed |
# | `tag_review_status` | Pending, accepted, rejected, or unresolved for a suggestion |
# | `effective_body_part` | The label currently adopted for catalog use |
# | `effective_label_origin` | Whether that label comes from the source or documented review |
# | `review_decision_id` | The decision supporting an adopted or blocked label |
# 
# Our precedence rules will be:
# 
# 1. An active, documented reviewed label takes precedence.
# 2. Otherwise, an acceptable source label may remain effective with its source origin and verification status.
# 3. A pending model suggestion does not automatically become effective.
# 4. An accepted suggestion becomes a reviewed catalog label only through a recorded decision.
# 5. An explicit decision rejecting a source label prevents automatic fallback to that rejected value.
# 
# A label can be valid within the catalog’s taxonomy while still awaiting independent source verification. We will preserve that distinction.
# 
# Model disagreement alone will not establish that a source label is wrong. Replacing an existing label will require an explicit review decision and supporting evidence.
# 
# Review decisions will record the reviewer, date, adopted value where applicable, reason, and evidence. Generating a pending worklist entry will not count as a completed human review.
# 
# Existing review history will be preserved. New input versions or model releases will receive traceable suggestion records rather than silently inherit earlier acceptance decisions.
# 
# The frozen Step 15 benchmark targets will remain separate from these catalog fields. Accepted suggestions will not become new training labels within the current experiment.
# 
# ### 22.9 Respect the Classifier’s Scope
# 
# The classifier will have learned from general exercise names and descriptions. Its results will not establish reliable transfer to every basketball drill.
# 
# We will preserve basketball skill categories such as shooting, passing, and ball handling. These describe a different labeling task from the classifier’s body-part categories.
# 
# The model will predict only among its frozen supported classes. A returned label will not prove that an unfamiliar exercise belongs within that class set.
# 
# Coverage flags and review will remain important for unfamiliar inputs. A high model score will not remove the review requirement.
# 
# Accepting a body-part tag will not change equipment requirements, participant counts, source instructions, youth suitability, or planner eligibility.
# 
# Those decisions will remain with the catalog and planning-rule review processes established earlier.
# 
# ### 22.10 Freeze the Catalog Handoff
# 
# We will preserve the classifier release, tagging decision, and derived catalog version supplied to later development steps.
# 
# Planner workflows using this component will receive the same identified model and catalog snapshot.
# 
# The Step 23 handoff will identify which records meet the separate requirements for retrieval and planner use. A predicted or accepted body-part tag alone will not satisfy those requirements.
# 
# If no records meet a required approval condition, we will report that limitation and preserve the open review work.
# 
# Before final evaluation, Step 31 will freeze the experiment’s model, catalog, and retrieval versions.
# 
# Any tagging of formerly held-out records after Step 32 will belong to a separate catalog revision. It will remain outside the frozen planner comparison rather than change the retrieval collection between classifier testing and planner scoring.
# 
# Later corrections will retain their history and identify the affected versions.
# 
# ### 22.11 Expected Outputs and Readiness
# 
# After completing this step, we expect to save:
# 
# | Output | Contents |
# |---|---|
# | `artifacts/classifiers/<release_id>/` | Versioned model bundle, supporting configurations, source package, and dependency information |
# | Bundle-local `manifest.json` | Artifact identities, hashes, selection decision, and supported scope |
# | `src/champion_athletic_map/classifier_inference.py` | Common loading and prediction interface |
# | `results/model_reload_checks.csv` | Fresh-process and intended-device verification results |
# | `results/exercise_tagging_population.csv` | Population screening and processed, skipped, or deferred records |
# | `data/processed/exercise_tag_predictions.csv` | Suggestions, model releases, input hashes, and handling flags |
# | `data/processed/exercise_catalog_tagged.csv` | Development catalog with label origins and review status preserved |
# | `results/exercise_tag_review.csv` | Preserved review history, pending suggestions, and actual decisions |
# | `docs/classifier_model_card.md` | Intended use, training data, selection evidence, loading instructions, and limitations |
# | `results/step22_step23_classifier_catalog_handoff.json` | Bundle and catalog references with retrieval-eligibility conditions |
# | `results/step22_classifier_packaging_summary.json` | Producer record, file hashes, checks, counts, and separate readiness states |
# 
# The summary will distinguish:
# 
# - Model-bundle verification.
# - Availability of the selected tagging model.
# - Tag-review completion.
# - Planner eligibility.
# 
# It will also report actual prediction and review counts and confirm that the original source catalog and frozen benchmark remain unchanged.
# 
# The model card will include validation findings available at this stage. Final test results will be added only after Step 32.
# 
# Step 23 will use the separately eligible reference material and catalog records to prepare the retrieval knowledge base.
# 
# 

# In[15]:


# Step 22-1 — Saving the Classifier and Tagging the Catalog: inputs and boundaries
# This cell verifies saved artifacts and metadata; it does not load models or tag records.
"""Verify the completed classifier-selection freeze before packaging any models."""


def load_step22_inputs(namespace):
    """Read saved metadata and bytes without deserializing or invoking a model."""
    import hashlib
    import io
    import json
    import math
    from pathlib import PurePosixPath

    import pandas as pd

    stage, checks = "completed_classifier_selection", []

    def packed(value):
        return (json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True, indent=2, allow_nan=False) + "\n").encode("utf-8")

    def sha(value):
        return hashlib.sha256(value).hexdigest()

    def check(name, condition, observed=True):
        nonlocal stage
        stage = name
        if not bool(condition):
            raise ValueError("classifier_packaging_input_condition_failed")
        checks.append({"check": name, "status": "pass", "observed": str(observed)})

    def number(value):
        actual = float(value)
        if not math.isfinite(actual):
            raise ValueError("nonfinite_saved_selection_number")
        return actual

    def equal_number(value, expected):
        return math.isclose(number(value), float(expected), rel_tol=1e-12, abs_tol=1e-15)

    try:
        check("completed_step21_selection_is_available", isinstance(namespace, dict)
              and namespace.get("step21_model_selection_ready") is True)
        stage = "frozen_search_dependencies"
        context = verify_step21_model_selection_inputs(namespace)
        checks.extend({"check": "complete_search:" + row["check"], "status": row["status"],
                       "observed": row["observed"]} for row in context["check_records"])
        root, inputs, runtime, plan = context["root"], context["inputs"], context["runtime"], context["plan_receipt"]

        def path(relative):
            if not isinstance(relative, str) or not relative or "\\" in relative or ":" in relative:
                raise ValueError("invalid_selection_dependency_path")
            parsed, target = PurePosixPath(relative), root / relative
            if (parsed.is_absolute() or parsed.as_posix() != relative
                    or any(part in (".", "..") for part in parsed.parts)
                    or target == root or target != target.resolve() or not target.is_relative_to(root)
                    or target.is_symlink() or not target.is_file()):
                raise ValueError("unsafe_selection_dependency_path")
            return target

        def content(relative):
            return path(relative).read_bytes()

        def json_object(relative):
            def pairs(items):
                value = {}
                for key, item in items:
                    if key in value:
                        raise ValueError("duplicate_saved_selection_json_key")
                    value[key] = item
                return value
            value = json.loads(content(relative), object_pairs_hook=pairs,
                parse_constant=lambda _value: (_ for _ in ()).throw(ValueError("nonfinite_selection_json")))
            if not isinstance(value, dict):
                raise ValueError("invalid_saved_selection_json")
            return value

        def frame(relative):
            result = pd.read_csv(io.BytesIO(content(relative)), dtype=str, keep_default_na=False)
            if not result.columns.is_unique:
                raise ValueError("duplicate_saved_selection_columns")
            return result

        summary_path, selection_path = "results/step21_model_selection_summary.json", "artifacts/model_selection.json"
        summary, selection = json_object(summary_path), json_object(selection_path)
        check("completed_selection_producer_matches_frozen_search", summary["schema_version"] == "step21-model-selection-producer-1"
              and summary["recipe_version"] == "fixed-search-model-selection-freeze-0.1.0"
              and summary["status"] == "classifier_models_selected_and_frozen"
              and summary["plan_id"] == plan["plan_id"] and summary["input_hashes"] == context["input_hashes"]
              and summary["model_selection_finalized"] is True)
        producer_keys = ("recipe_version", "plan_id", "input_hashes", "selection_digest", "reference_replay_digest",
                         "diagnostics_digest", "selection_probe_digest", "output_hashes")
        producer_identity = {key: summary[key] for key in producer_keys}
        check("completed_selection_producer_identity", summary["producer_id"]
              == "classifier-model-selection-freeze:" + sha(packed(producer_identity)))
        selection_identity = {key: value for key, value in selection.items()
                              if key not in ("schema_version", "selection_id", "selection_digest", "status")}
        selection_digest = sha(packed(selection_identity))
        check("completed_model_selection_identity", selection["schema_version"] == "classifier-model-selection-1"
              and selection["recipe_version"] == "fixed-search-final-model-selection-0.1.0"
              and selection["status"] == "selected_models_frozen_for_packaging"
              and selection["selection_digest"] == summary["selection_digest"] == selection_digest
              and selection["selection_id"] == "classifier-model-selection:" + selection_digest
              and selection["plan_id"] == plan["plan_id"] and selection["plan_digest"] == plan["plan_digest"]
              and selection["input_hashes"] == context["input_hashes"])
        check("selection_producer_and_record_keep_stable_json", content(summary_path) == packed(summary)
              and content(selection_path) == packed(selection))
        live = namespace.get("step21_model_selection")
        if live is not None:
            check("live_selection_receipt_matches_saved_freeze", isinstance(live, dict)
                  and live.get("summary") == summary and live.get("model_selection_finalized") is True
                  and isinstance(live.get("decision"), dict) and live["decision"].get("selection_record") == selection)
        check("packaging_handoff_preserves_open_evaluation_boundaries", all(selection[key] is True for key in
              ("model_selection_finalized", "models_frozen", "selected_artifacts_ready_for_packaging",
               "validation_scores_are_development_evidence", "planner_acceptance_remains_pending"))
              and all(selection[key] is False for key in ("training_and_validation_refit", "test_text_processed",
                  "classifier_packaging_complete", "catalog_labels_changed", "full_step17_operational_protocol_ready",
                  "final_classifier_scoring_ready"))
              and selection["final_held_out_evaluation_step"] == summary["final_test_evaluation_owner_step"] == 32
              and summary["packaging_owner_step"] == 22
              and all(summary[key] is False for key in ("test_text_processed", "training_plus_validation_refit",
                  "catalog_labels_changed", "planner_eligibility_changed", "final_classifier_scoring_completed"))
              and summary["new_logistic_fit_attempts"] == summary["new_neural_training_runs"] == summary["vocabulary_or_sequence_refits"] == 0)
        expected_outputs = {selection_path, "results/tuning/candidate_runs.csv", "results/tuning/validation_metrics.csv",
            "results/tuning/selected_validation_metrics.csv", "results/tuning/selected_validation_predictions.csv",
            "results/tuning/selected_validation_class_report.csv", "results/tuning/selection_checks.csv",
            "docs/model_selection_summary.md", "results/tuning/selected_confusion_counts.csv",
            "results/tuning/selected_confusion_row_normalized.csv", "results/tuning/selected_subset_diagnostics.csv",
            "results/tuning/selected_neural_learning_history.csv", "reports/figures/step21_selected_confusion_counts.png",
            "reports/figures/step21_selected_confusion_row_normalized.png", "reports/figures/step21_selected_neural_learning.png"}
        check("final_selection_output_manifest_has_exact_scope", set(summary["output_hashes"]) == expected_outputs
              and not (expected_outputs & set(context["input_hashes"])))
        stage = "final_selection_output_bytes"
        stage_hashes = {}
        for relative, expected in summary["output_hashes"].items():
            if sha(content(relative)) != expected:
                raise ValueError("saved_final_selection_artifact_changed")
            stage_hashes[relative] = expected
        stage_hashes[summary_path] = sha(content(summary_path))
        check("all_final_selection_payloads_and_producer_are_bound", len(stage_hashes) == len(expected_outputs) + 1, len(stage_hashes))

        classes, validation = inputs["class_order"], inputs["validation"]
        check("frozen_benchmark_preprocessing_and_class_binding", selection["benchmark_id"] == inputs["benchmark_id"]
              and selection["preprocessing_id"] == inputs["preprocessing_id"]
              and selection["class_order"] == classes and selection["class_to_index"] == inputs["class_to_index"]
              and all(selection[key] == plan["plan"]["bindings"][key] for key in (
                  "ordered_training_ids_sha256", "ordered_validation_ids_sha256", "development_table_hashes")))
        fixed_paths = {"artifacts/splits/exercise_split_config.json", "artifacts/preprocessing/preprocessing_config.json",
            "artifacts/preprocessing/label_mapping.json", "artifacts/preprocessing/neural_vocabulary.json",
            "src/champion_athletic_map/text_preprocessing.py", "src/champion_athletic_map/neural_classifier.py"}
        check("frozen_preprocessing_and_source_dependencies_are_identified", set(selection["fixed_inputs"]) == fixed_paths
              and all(spec == {"relative_path": relative, "sha256": context["input_hashes"][relative]}
                      for relative, spec in selection["fixed_inputs"].items()))
        models = selection["selected_models"]
        check("three_research_artifacts_are_frozen", set(models) == {"majority", "logistic_regression", "neural"}
              and all(spec["seed"] == 42 and spec["fit_partition"] == "train" and spec["retrained_after_selection"] is False
                      for spec in models.values()))
        for role, spec in models.items():
            for key in ("model", "configuration", "producer", "module"):
                if key not in spec:
                    continue
                binding = spec[key]
                check("selected_artifact_source_bytes:" + role + ":" + key,
                      set(binding) == {"relative_path", "sha256"}
                      and binding["relative_path"] in context["input_hashes"]
                      and binding["sha256"] == context["input_hashes"][binding["relative_path"]])
        majority = inputs["baseline_config"]["models"]["majority_class"]
        check("majority_reference_preserves_original_training_fit", models["majority"]["model_id"] == "majority_class"
              and all(models["majority"][key] == majority[key] for key in ("configuration_id", "run_id"))
              and models["majority"]["model"]["relative_path"] == majority["relative_path"]
              and models["majority"]["fitted_state_sha256"] == majority["model_state_sha256"]
              and models["majority"]["validation_macro_f1"] == inputs["baseline_metric_summaries"]["majority_class"]["macro_f1"])
        logistic_id, neural_id = models["logistic_regression"]["candidate_id"], models["neural"]["candidate_id"]
        logistic_summary, initial = context["logistic_summary"], context["initial_summary"]
        check("selected_logistic_remains_the_frozen_family_leader", selection["logistic_ranking"] == logistic_summary["ranking"]
              and logistic_id == logistic_summary["leading_logistic_candidate"] == logistic_summary["ranking"]["ranking"][0]["candidate_id"]
              and models["logistic_regression"]["validation_macro_f1"] == logistic_summary["ranking"]["ranking"][0]["macro_f1"])
        check("selected_neural_remains_the_complete_seed_mean_choice", selection["neural_selection"] == context["comparison"]["selection"]
              and selection["neural_seed_summaries"] == context["comparison"]["seed_summaries"]
              and selection["neural_shortlist"] == context["shortlist"]
              and neural_id == context["comparison"]["selected_configuration"]["candidate_id"]
              and selection["primary_neural_artifact_seed"] == models["neural"]["seed"] == 42
              and models["neural"]["highest_scoring_seed_selected"] is models["neural"]["ensemble_used"] is False)
        selected_metrics = {"majority": inputs["baseline_metric_summaries"]["majority_class"]}
        source_metadata = {"majority": {"configuration": inputs["baseline_config"], "model_spec": majority}}
        for role, rows, metrics_rows in (("logistic_regression", logistic_summary["candidate_runs"], logistic_summary["validation_metrics"]),
                                        ("neural", initial["initial_runs"], initial["validation_metrics"])):
            spec = models[role]
            row = next(row for row in rows if row["candidate_id"] == spec["candidate_id"])
            metric = next(row for row in metrics_rows if row["candidate_id"] == spec["candidate_id"])
            check("selected_configuration_run_and_score_match_source:" + role,
                  all(spec[key] == row[key] for key in ("candidate_id", "configuration_id", "run_id", "candidate_digest", "origin_step"))
                  and spec["model"]["relative_path"] == row["saved_model_path"]
                  and spec["validation_macro_f1"] == metric["macro_f1"]
                  and spec["validation_accuracy"] == metric["accuracy"])
            if spec["candidate_id"] == "L2":
                source = inputs["baseline_config"]["models"]["tfidf_logistic_regression"]
                metrics = inputs["baseline_metric_summaries"]["tfidf_logistic_regression"]
                native = {"configuration": inputs["baseline_config"], "model_spec": source}
                state_digest = source["model_state_sha256"]
            elif spec["candidate_id"] == "N0":
                source = inputs["neural_config"]
                metrics = inputs["neural_metric_summary"]
                native = {"configuration": source, "model_spec": spec}
                state_digest = source["best_state_digest"]
            else:
                source = json_object(spec["configuration"]["relative_path"])
                snapshot = source["receipt_snapshot"]
                metrics = snapshot["metrics"]
                native = {"configuration": source, "receipt_snapshot": snapshot, "model_spec": spec}
                state_digest = snapshot["model_state_sha256"] if role == "logistic_regression" else snapshot["best_state_digest"]
            check("selected_metrics_and_fitted_state_metadata_are_bound:" + role,
                  metrics["status"] == "available" and metrics["class_order"] == classes
                  and metrics["n_records"] == len(validation) and metrics["n_groups"] == int(validation["split_group_id"].nunique())
                  and metrics["macro_f1"] == metric["macro_f1"] and metrics["accuracy"] == metric["accuracy"]
                  and spec["fitted_state_sha256"] == state_digest)
            if role == "neural":
                chosen = context["comparison"]["selected_configuration"]
                seed_summary = next(item for item in context["comparison"]["seed_summaries"] if item["candidate_id"] == neural_id)
                check("neural_seed42_epoch_and_complete_seed_evidence_are_preserved", spec["best_epoch"] == row["best_epoch"] == chosen["best_epoch"]
                      and spec["fitted_state_sha256"] == row["best_state_digest"]
                      and spec["configuration_mean_macro_f1"] == seed_summary["mean_macro_f1"]
                      and spec["configuration_sample_standard_deviation"] == seed_summary["sample_standard_deviation"]
                      and spec["configuration_seed_scores"] == dict(zip(("42", "17", "73"), seed_summary["scores"]))
                      and spec["standard_deviation_ddof"] == 1)
            selected_metrics[role], source_metadata[role] = metrics, native
        tagging = selection["tagging_model"]
        expected_tagging = choose_step21_tagging_artifact(models["logistic_regression"]["validation_macro_f1"],
            models["neural"]["validation_macro_f1"], models["majority"]["validation_macro_f1"], True)
        check("tagging_decision_preserves_actual_artifact_comparison", summary["tagging_decision"] == tagging
              and all(tagging[key] == expected_tagging[key] for key in ("status", "model_family", "macro_f1"))
              and tagging["status"] in ("selected", "disabled") and tagging["neural_three_seed_mean_used_for_tagging"] is False
              and tagging["catalog_predictions_are_suggestions"] is True and tagging["exercise_or_drill_approval_granted"] is False)
        if tagging["status"] == "selected":
            spec = models[tagging["model_family"]]
            check("selected_tagging_model_has_exact_frozen_identity", all(tagging[key] == spec[key] for key in
                  ("candidate_id", "configuration_id", "run_id", "model")) and tagging["macro_f1"] > tagging["majority_macro_f1"])

        tables = {relative: frame(relative) for relative in expected_outputs if relative.endswith(".csv")}
        candidates, metrics_table = tables["results/tuning/candidate_runs.csv"], tables["results/tuning/validation_metrics.csv"]
        scheduled = [("logistic_regression", row, metric) for row, metric in zip(logistic_summary["candidate_runs"], logistic_summary["validation_metrics"])]
        scheduled += [("neural", row, metric) for row, metric in zip(initial["initial_runs"], initial["validation_metrics"])]
        repeated_runs = {(row["candidate_id"], row["seed"]): row for row in context["repetition_summary"]["per_seed_runs"]}
        repeated_metrics = {(row["candidate_id"], row["seed"]): row for row in context["repetition_summary"]["validation_metrics"]}
        scheduled += [("neural", repeated_runs[(item["candidate_id"], item["seed"])], repeated_metrics[(item["candidate_id"], item["seed"])])
                      for item in context["repetition_schedule"]]
        slots = [(family, row["candidate_id"], row["seed"]) for family, row, metric in scheduled]
        check("consolidated_candidate_and_metric_tables_keep_all_scheduled_outcomes", len(candidates) == len(metrics_table) == len(slots) == 14
              and [(row["family"], row["candidate_id"], int(row["seed"])) for row in candidates.to_dict("records")] == slots
              and [(row["family"], row["candidate_id"], int(row["seed"])) for row in metrics_table.to_dict("records")] == slots)
        check("consolidated_statuses_and_scores_match_recorded_search", all(
              saved["status"] == saved_metric["status"] == source["status"] == source_metric["status"]
              and saved["configuration_id"] == source["configuration_id"] and saved["run_id"] == source["run_id"]
              and ((saved_metric["macro_f1"] == saved_metric["accuracy"] == "") if source_metric["macro_f1"] is None else
                   equal_number(saved_metric["macro_f1"], source_metric["macro_f1"])
                   and equal_number(saved_metric["accuracy"], source_metric["accuracy"]))
              for saved, saved_metric, (_, source, source_metric) in zip(candidates.to_dict("records"), metrics_table.to_dict("records"), scheduled)))
        selected_table = tables["results/tuning/selected_validation_metrics.csv"]
        check("three_selected_metric_rows_keep_the_frozen_populations", selected_table["artifact_role"].tolist()
              == ["majority", "logistic_regression", "neural"] and len(selected_table) == 3
              and all(row["configuration_id"] == models[row["artifact_role"]]["configuration_id"]
                  and row["run_id"] == models[row["artifact_role"]]["run_id"]
                  and int(row["records"]) == len(validation) and int(row["class_denominator"]) == len(classes)
                  and equal_number(row["macro_f1"], models[row["artifact_role"]]["validation_macro_f1"])
                  and equal_number(row["accuracy"], models[row["artifact_role"]]["validation_accuracy"])
                  for row in selected_table.to_dict("records")))
        predictions = tables["results/tuning/selected_validation_predictions.csv"]
        class_report = tables["results/tuning/selected_validation_class_report.csv"]
        roles = {"majority_class": "majority", "selected_logistic": "logistic_regression", "selected_neural": "neural"}
        check("selected_prediction_and_class_report_populations", len(predictions) == len(roles) * len(validation)
              and len(class_report) == len(roles) * len(classes)
              and set(predictions["comparison_role"]) == set(class_report["comparison_role"]) == set(roles))
        for role, model_role in roles.items():
            spec, metrics = models[model_role], selected_metrics[model_role]
            predicted = predictions.loc[predictions["comparison_role"].eq(role)]
            report = class_report.loc[class_report["comparison_role"].eq(role)]
            probability_columns = ["prob_class_" + str(index) for index in range(len(classes))]
            check("saved_prediction_alignment_and_class_decoding:" + role,
                  len(predicted) == len(validation) and all(predicted[key].tolist() == validation[key].astype(str).tolist()
                      for key in ("catalog_id", "split_group_id", "split", "target_label", "text_availability"))
                  and predicted["configuration_id"].eq(spec["configuration_id"]).all()
                  and predicted["run_id"].eq(spec["run_id"]).all()
                  and predicted["model_id"].eq(spec["model_id"]).all() and predicted["seed"].eq("42").all()
                  and all(classes[int(index)] == label for index, label in zip(predicted["predicted_class_index"], predicted["predicted_label"]))
                  and all(column in predicted for column in probability_columns)
                  and all(all(0 <= number(row[key]) <= 1 for key in probability_columns)
                      and math.isclose(sum(number(row[key]) for key in probability_columns), 1, rel_tol=1e-5, abs_tol=1e-6)
                      for row in predicted.to_dict("records")))
            check("saved_class_report_axes_and_values:" + role, report["class_index"].astype(int).tolist() == list(range(len(classes)))
                  and report["label"].tolist() == classes
                  and all(equal_number(saved[key], expected[key]) for saved, expected in zip(report.to_dict("records"), metrics["per_class"])
                      for key in ("precision", "recall", "f1", "support_records", "support_groups", "predicted_records"))
                  and all(saved[key] == str(expected[key]) for saved, expected in zip(report.to_dict("records"), metrics["per_class"])
                      for key in ("precision_defined", "recall_defined", "f1_defined")))
        ledger = tables["results/tuning/selection_checks.csv"]
        check("saved_selection_checks_are_complete_and_passing", not ledger.empty and len(ledger) == summary["saved_check_records"]
              and ledger["status"].eq("pass").all(), len(ledger))
        check("selected_confusion_and_history_outputs_keep_expected_axes", len(tables["results/tuning/selected_confusion_counts.csv"])
              == len(tables["results/tuning/selected_confusion_row_normalized.csv"]) == len(roles) * len(classes) ** 2
              and len(tables["results/tuning/selected_neural_learning_history.csv"])
                  == next(row for row in initial["initial_runs"] if row["candidate_id"] == neural_id)["epochs_completed"])
        check("selection_figures_and_plain_language_handoff_are_present", all(content(relative).startswith(b"\x89PNG\r\n\x1a\n")
              for relative in expected_outputs if relative.endswith(".png"))
              and content("docs/model_selection_summary.md").startswith(b"# Step 21"))
        check("saved_search_counts_match_final_freeze", selection["run_counts"]["scheduled_candidate_seed_outcomes"] == len(slots)
              and selection["run_counts"]["unfinished_or_unresolved_outcomes"] == 0
              and selection["run_counts"]["recorded_step21_logistic_fitting_attempts"]
                  == summary["recorded_step21_logistic_fit_attempts"] == logistic_summary["recorded_step21_logistic_fit_attempts"]
              and selection["run_counts"]["recorded_new_neural_runs_in_step21"] == summary["recorded_step21_neural_training_runs"]
              and summary["selected_logistic_candidate"] == logistic_id and summary["selected_neural_configuration"] == neural_id
              and summary["selected_neural_primary_seed"] == models["neural"]["seed"] == 42
              and summary["selected_neural_best_epoch"] == models["neural"]["best_epoch"])

        input_hashes = {**context["input_hashes"], **stage_hashes}
        frozen_metadata = {"selection": selection, "summary": summary, "selected_models": models,
            "tagging_decision": tagging, "selected_model_metadata": source_metadata,
            "selected_model_metrics": selected_metrics}
        metadata_digest = sha(packed(frozen_metadata))
        frozen_tables = {relative: sha(table.to_csv(index=False, lineterminator="\n").encode("utf-8")) for relative, table in tables.items()}

        def verify_unchanged():
            context["verify_unchanged"]()
            for relative, expected in stage_hashes.items():
                if sha(content(relative)) != expected:
                    raise RuntimeError("step22_input_verification_failed:frozen_selection_file_changed")
            if (sha(packed(frozen_metadata)) != metadata_digest
                    or input_hashes != {**context["input_hashes"], **stage_hashes}
                    or any(sha(tables[relative].to_csv(index=False, lineterminator="\n").encode("utf-8")) != expected
                           for relative, expected in frozen_tables.items())):
                raise RuntimeError("step22_input_verification_failed:prepared_selection_metadata_changed")
            return True

        verify_unchanged()
        check("all_prior_classifier_search_and_freeze_files_remain_unchanged", True, len(input_hashes))
        model_rows = [{"artifact_role": role, "candidate_id": spec["candidate_id"], "model_id": spec["model_id"],
            "seed": spec["seed"], "best_epoch": spec.get("best_epoch"), "validation_accuracy": spec["validation_accuracy"],
            "validation_macro_f1": spec["validation_macro_f1"], "fit_partition": spec["fit_partition"],
            "model_path": spec["model"]["relative_path"], "model_sha256": spec["model"]["sha256"]} for role, spec in models.items()]
        return {**context, "status": "selected_classifier_packaging_inputs_verified", "selection_context": context,
            "selection_record": selection, "selection_summary": summary, "selected_models": models,
            "selected_model_metadata": source_metadata, "selected_model_metrics": selected_metrics,
            "tagging_decision": tagging, "selected_artifacts": pd.DataFrame(model_rows), "selection_tables": tables,
            "selection_stage_hashes": stage_hashes, "input_hashes": input_hashes,
            "planned_reference_runtime": runtime["runtime"], "checks": pd.DataFrame(checks), "check_records": checks,
            "verify_unchanged": verify_unchanged, "models_loaded": 0, "model_predictions": 0, "model_fits": 0,
            "new_neural_training_runs": 0, "vocabulary_refitted": False, "sequence_limit_refitted": False,
            "test_text_processed": False, "files_changed": False, "catalog_labels_changed": False,
            "classifier_bundle_verified": False, "tag_review_completed": False, "planner_acceptance_remains_pending": True}
    except Exception as error:
        message = str(error)
        if message.startswith(("step21_", "step20_", "step19_", "step22_")):
            raise RuntimeError(message) from None
        raise RuntimeError("step22_input_verification_failed:" + stage) from None


"""Prepare the catalog population boundary from frozen split metadata only."""


def _step22_partition_population_metadata(records):
    """Assign every record once, protecting held-out groups before eligibility."""
    columns = {"catalog_id", "split_group_id", "benchmark_eligible", "split"}
    if not isinstance(records, list):
        raise ValueError("invalid_population_metadata")
    identifiers, active_groups = set(), {}
    for row in records:
        if (not isinstance(row, dict) or set(row) != columns
                or not all(isinstance(row[key], str) for key in columns)
                or not row["catalog_id"] or not row["split_group_id"]
                or row["catalog_id"] in identifiers or row["benchmark_eligible"] not in ("yes", "no")
                or (row["benchmark_eligible"] == "yes" and row["split"] not in ("train", "validation", "test"))
                or (row["benchmark_eligible"] == "no" and row["split"] != "")):
            raise ValueError("invalid_population_metadata")
        identifiers.add(row["catalog_id"])
        if row["benchmark_eligible"] == "yes":
            active_groups.setdefault(row["split_group_id"], set()).add(row["split"])
    if any(len(splits) != 1 for splits in active_groups.values()):
        raise ValueError("eligible_group_crosses_frozen_splits")
    protected_groups = frozenset(group for group, splits in active_groups.items() if "test" in splits)
    categories = []
    for row in records:
        if row["split_group_id"] in protected_groups:
            category = "protected_test_group"
        elif row["benchmark_eligible"] == "yes" and row["split"] == "train":
            category = "training_preview"
        elif row["benchmark_eligible"] == "yes" and row["split"] == "validation":
            category = "validation_preview"
        else:
            category = "other_excluded_review_only"
        categories.append(category)
    return {"categories": categories, "protected_groups": protected_groups}


def prepare_step22_population_boundary(inputs_receipt):
    """Read only frozen identifiers, groups and split flags; prepare no suggestions.

    The ``private_boundary`` return value is for later screening.  It is not an
    export, worklist or public diagnostic table.  Public summaries contain only
    aggregate counts and hashes.  This component never reads exercise text.
    """
    import hashlib
    import io
    import json
    from pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath
    import pandas as pd

    stage, checks = "verified_packaging_inputs", []

    def packed(value):
        return (json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True, indent=2, allow_nan=False) + "\n").encode("utf-8")

    def sha(value):
        return hashlib.sha256(value).hexdigest()

    def check(name, condition, observed=True):
        nonlocal stage
        stage = name
        if not bool(condition):
            raise ValueError("population_boundary_condition_failed")
        checks.append({"check": name, "status": "pass", "observed": str(observed)})

    try:
        check("verified_input_receipt_available", isinstance(inputs_receipt, dict)
              and isinstance(inputs_receipt.get("input_hashes"), dict)
              and callable(inputs_receipt.get("verify_unchanged")))
        inputs = inputs_receipt["inputs"]
        root = Path(inputs_receipt.get("root", inputs["root"])).resolve(strict=True)
        upstream_verify = inputs_receipt["verify_unchanged"]
        upstream_verify()
        hashes = dict(inputs_receipt["input_hashes"])

        def content(relative):
            if not isinstance(relative, str) or relative not in hashes or "\\" in relative or ":" in relative:
                raise ValueError("unbound_population_dependency")
            parsed, target = PurePosixPath(relative), root / relative
            if (parsed.is_absolute() or parsed.as_posix() != relative
                    or any(part in (".", "..") for part in parsed.parts)
                    or target == root or target.resolve() != target or target.is_symlink() or not target.is_file()):
                raise ValueError("unsafe_population_dependency_path")
            payload = target.read_bytes()
            if sha(payload) != hashes[relative]:
                raise ValueError("population_dependency_bytes_changed")
            return payload

        summary_path = "results/step15_exercise_split_summary.json"
        summary_bytes = content(summary_path)
        frozen = json.loads(summary_bytes)
        class_order = list(inputs["class_order"])
        check("frozen_benchmark_population_binding", frozen["schema_version"] == "step15-exercise-split-1"
              and frozen["status"] == "frozen" and frozen["benchmark_frozen"] is True
              and frozen["benchmark_id"] == inputs["benchmark_id"]
              and frozen["class_order"] == class_order and len(class_order) == 16
              and frozen["class_to_index"] == {label: index for index, label in enumerate(class_order)})
        manifest_candidates = [relative for relative, spec in frozen["artifacts"].items()
            if PurePosixPath(relative).name == "exercise_split_manifest.csv" and spec.get("kind") == "csv"]
        check("unique_frozen_split_manifest", len(manifest_candidates) == 1)
        manifest_path = manifest_candidates[0]
        manifest_bytes = content(manifest_path)
        spec = frozen["artifacts"][manifest_path]
        columns = ["catalog_id", "split_group_id", "benchmark_eligible", "split"]
        check("frozen_manifest_bytes_and_metadata_columns", spec["sha256"] == hashes[manifest_path]
              and spec["bytes"] == len(manifest_bytes) and len(spec["columns"]) == len(set(spec["columns"]))
              and set(columns).issubset(spec["columns"]))
        metadata = pd.read_csv(io.BytesIO(manifest_bytes), usecols=columns,
            dtype=str, keep_default_na=False, encoding="utf-8-sig")[columns]
        check("frozen_manifest_metadata_schema", metadata.columns.tolist() == columns
              and len(metadata) == spec["rows"] == frozen["population"]["source_records"] == 2909)
        stage = "whole_group_protection_before_record_eligibility"
        records = metadata.to_dict("records")
        partition = _step22_partition_population_metadata(records)
        categories, protected_groups = partition["categories"], partition["protected_groups"]
        active = metadata.loc[metadata["benchmark_eligible"].eq("yes")]
        excluded = metadata.loc[metadata["benchmark_eligible"].eq("no")]
        check("frozen_eligible_and_excluded_populations", len(active) == frozen["population"]["eligible_records"] == 2872
              and len(excluded) == frozen["population"]["excluded_records"] == 37
              and active["split_group_id"].nunique() == frozen["population"]["eligible_groups"])
        expected = {"train": (1999, 1794), "validation": (435, 384), "test": (438, 385)}
        for split, (record_count, group_count) in expected.items():
            selected = active.loc[active["split"].eq(split)]
            check("frozen_split_metadata_population:" + split,
                  len(selected) == record_count and selected["split_group_id"].nunique() == group_count,
                  str(record_count) + " records; " + str(group_count) + " groups")
        check("protected_group_set_comes_only_from_frozen_test_membership", protected_groups
              == frozenset(active.loc[active["split"].eq("test"), "split_group_id"]))
        keys = ["training_preview", "validation_preview", "protected_test_group", "other_excluded_review_only"]
        category_ids = {key: tuple(row["catalog_id"] for row, category in zip(records, categories) if category == key) for key in keys}
        category_groups = {key: frozenset(row["split_group_id"] for row, category in zip(records, categories) if category == key) for key in keys}
        protected_ids = frozenset(category_ids["protected_test_group"])
        development_ids = frozenset(category_ids["training_preview"] + category_ids["validation_preview"])
        protected_eligible = sum(row["benchmark_eligible"] == "yes" and category == "protected_test_group"
            for row, category in zip(records, categories))
        protected_excluded = sum(row["benchmark_eligible"] == "no" and category == "protected_test_group"
            for row, category in zip(records, categories))
        check("all_catalog_records_have_one_population_category", len(categories) == len(records)
              and sum(len(value) for value in category_ids.values()) == len(records)
              and len(set().union(*(set(value) for value in category_ids.values()))) == len(records))
        check("eligible_development_previews_are_disjoint_from_protected_groups",
              len(category_ids["training_preview"]) == len(inputs["train"]) == 1999
              and len(category_ids["validation_preview"]) == len(inputs["validation"]) == 435
              and category_ids["training_preview"] == tuple(inputs["train"]["catalog_id"])
              and category_ids["validation_preview"] == tuple(inputs["validation"]["catalog_id"])
              and development_ids.isdisjoint(protected_ids)
              and category_groups["training_preview"].isdisjoint(protected_groups)
              and category_groups["validation_preview"].isdisjoint(protected_groups))
        check("protected_boundary_includes_every_group_related_excluded_record", protected_eligible == expected["test"][0]
              and len(protected_ids) == protected_eligible + protected_excluded
              and all((category == "protected_test_group") == (row["split_group_id"] in protected_groups)
                      for row, category in zip(records, categories)))
        check("other_excluded_records_are_not_development_previews", len(category_ids["other_excluded_review_only"])
              == len(excluded) - protected_excluded
              and all(row["benchmark_eligible"] == "no" for row, category in zip(records, categories)
                      if category == "other_excluded_review_only"))
        private_boundary = {"protected_catalog_ids": protected_ids, "protected_group_ids": protected_groups,
            "training_preview_catalog_ids": category_ids["training_preview"],
            "validation_preview_catalog_ids": category_ids["validation_preview"],
            "other_excluded_catalog_ids": frozenset(category_ids["other_excluded_review_only"])}
        actions = {"training_preview": "planned_in_sample_preview", "validation_preview": "planned_development_preview",
            "protected_test_group": "deferred_until_final_classifier_evaluation",
            "other_excluded_review_only": "review_required_not_in_initial_preview_population"}
        summary_rows = [{"population": key, "records": len(category_ids[key]), "groups": len(category_groups[key]),
            "planned_action": actions[key], "eligible_for_initial_development_preview": key in ("training_preview", "validation_preview"),
            "predictions_produced": 0} for key in keys]
        summary_df = pd.DataFrame(summary_rows)
        count_summary = {"catalog_records": len(records), "benchmark_eligible_records": len(active),
            "benchmark_excluded_records": len(excluded), "eligible_training_preview_records": len(category_ids["training_preview"]),
            "eligible_validation_preview_records": len(category_ids["validation_preview"]),
            "eligible_development_preview_records": len(development_ids), "eligible_test_records": protected_eligible,
            "protected_test_groups": len(protected_groups), "all_protected_group_records": len(protected_ids),
            "excluded_records_in_protected_test_groups": protected_excluded,
            "other_excluded_review_only_records": len(category_ids["other_excluded_review_only"]),
            "new_record_population_selected": False, "new_record_screening_executed": False,
            "catalog_predictions_produced": 0, "source_catalog_text_read": False,
            "protected_text_read_or_transformed": False, "catalog_labels_changed": False}
        identity = {"recipe_version": "frozen-exercise-population-boundary-0.1.0",
            "benchmark_id": inputs["benchmark_id"], "manifest": {"relative_path": manifest_path, "sha256": hashes[manifest_path]},
            "metadata_columns_read": columns, "count_summary": count_summary, "population_rows": summary_rows,
            "whole_protected_group_membership_takes_precedence": True,
            "new_records_matching_or_maybe_matching_protected_groups": "defer_without_tagging",
            "new_record_grouping_policy": "use_existing_conservative_frozen_grouping_policy; do_not_reassign_benchmark_splits",
            "preview_outputs_are_not_generalization_evidence": True,
            "held_out_tagging_after_step32_requires_a_separate_catalog_revision": True,
            "protected_identities_exported": False, "public_outputs_contain_aggregate_counts_only": True}

        def private_snapshot():
            return {key: list(value) if isinstance(value, tuple) else sorted(value)
                    for key, value in private_boundary.items()}

        metadata_sha = sha(metadata.to_csv(index=False, lineterminator="\n").encode("utf-8"))
        private_sha = sha(packed(private_snapshot()))
        identity_sha = sha(packed(identity))
        summary_sha = sha(summary_df.to_csv(index=False, lineterminator="\n").encode("utf-8"))
        class_snapshot = tuple(class_order)

        def verify_unchanged():
            upstream_verify()
            if (content(summary_path) != summary_bytes or content(manifest_path) != manifest_bytes
                    or dict(inputs_receipt["input_hashes"]) != hashes
                    or tuple(inputs["class_order"]) != class_snapshot
                    or sha(metadata.to_csv(index=False, lineterminator="\n").encode("utf-8")) != metadata_sha
                    or sha(packed(private_snapshot())) != private_sha or sha(packed(identity)) != identity_sha
                    or sha(summary_df.to_csv(index=False, lineterminator="\n").encode("utf-8")) != summary_sha):
                raise RuntimeError("step22_population_boundary_failed:frozen_population_metadata_changed")
            return True

        check("public_boundary_summary_contains_no_record_or_group_identifiers", set(summary_df.columns)
              == {"population", "records", "groups", "planned_action", "eligible_for_initial_development_preview", "predictions_produced"}
              and count_summary["catalog_predictions_produced"] == 0)
        check("prepared_population_boundary_is_read_only", verify_unchanged())
        return {"status": "frozen_catalog_population_boundary_prepared", "root": root,
            "manifest_path": manifest_path, "manifest_sha256": hashes[manifest_path],
            "summary_df": summary_df, "summary_records": summary_rows, "count_summary": count_summary,
            "boundary_identity": identity, "boundary_digest": identity_sha,
            "private_boundary": private_boundary, "checks": pd.DataFrame(checks), "check_records": checks,
            "verify_unchanged": verify_unchanged, "new_record_population_selected": False,
            "new_record_screening_executed": False, "source_catalog_text_read": False,
            "protected_text_read_or_transformed": False, "catalog_predictions_produced": 0,
            "models_created": 0, "models_loaded": 0, "files_changed": False}
    except Exception as error:
        message = str(error)
        if message.startswith("step22_"):
            raise RuntimeError(message) from None
        raise RuntimeError("step22_population_boundary_failed:" + stage) from None


def run_step22_population_boundary_probes():
    """Check group precedence and rejection using authored metadata only."""
    import hashlib
    import json
    import pandas as pd

    scenarios, checks = [], []

    def row(identifier, group, eligible="yes", split="train"):
        return {"catalog_id": identifier, "split_group_id": group, "benchmark_eligible": eligible, "split": split}

    def probe(name, condition):
        if not bool(condition):
            raise RuntimeError("step22_population_probe_failed:" + name)
        scenarios.append(name)
        checks.append({"check": name, "status": "pass", "observed": "True"})

    def rejected(records):
        try:
            _step22_partition_population_metadata(records)
        except (ValueError, TypeError, KeyError):
            return True
        return False

    records = [row("training_example", "g_train"), row("validation_example", "g_validation", split="validation"),
        row("held_out_example", "g_test", split="test"), row("excluded_relative", "g_test", "no", ""),
        row("excluded_other", "g_other", "no", "")]
    result = _step22_partition_population_metadata(records)
    probe("excluded_member_of_a_test_group_is_protected_before_eligibility", result["categories"][3] == "protected_test_group")
    probe("excluded_nonprotected_record_is_review_only", result["categories"][4] == "other_excluded_review_only")
    probe("eligible_development_records_remain_separate_previews", result["categories"][:2] == ["training_preview", "validation_preview"])
    probe("eligible_group_crossing_training_and_test_is_rejected", rejected([row("a", "g"), row("b", "g", split="test")]))
    probe("duplicate_catalog_identity_is_rejected", rejected([row("a", "g1"), row("a", "g2")]))
    probe("unassigned_eligible_split_is_rejected", rejected([row("a", "g", split="")]))
    probe("excluded_record_with_adopted_split_is_rejected", rejected([row("a", "g", "no", "train")]))
    probe("metadata_classifier_rejects_text_fields", rejected([{**row("a", "g"), "exercise_name": "authored example"}]))
    identity = {"scenarios": scenarios, "checks": checks}
    digest = hashlib.sha256((json.dumps(identity, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + "\n").encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()
    return {"status": "population_boundary_artificial_checks_passed", "scenario_count": len(scenarios),
        "checks": pd.DataFrame(checks), "check_records": checks, "probe_digest": digest,
        "models_created": 0, "catalog_text_read": False, "files_changed": False}


