# 
# The research bundle preserves the three artifacts selected earlier, with their original training-partition fits.
# 
# | Artifact | Preserved form | Role |
# |---|---|---|
# | Majority-class baseline | Fitted training-derived constant predictor | Research comparison |
# | Logistic regression L5 | Complete fitted text-preparation, TF-IDF, and classification pipeline | Selected tagging model and research comparison |
# | Neural N3 | Selected seed-42 state dictionary, best epoch 19, with architecture configuration | Research comparison |
# 
# The release is `exercise-classifier-4f6b6f435ef52fef8f4cca6d`. Its 17 bundle-local files include the models, required source package, frozen preprocessing dependencies, vocabulary, sequence settings, class mapping, environment information, and manifest. Relative paths and actual file hashes identify the packaged contents. External producer records bind the completed manifest and verification evidence.
# 
# Packaging retained the Step 21 selection. No model was refitted, no alternative neural seed or checkpoint was substituted, and training and validation data were not combined. The neural state dictionary supports inference and evaluation; it is not a complete checkpoint for resuming the exact training process.
# 
# #### 2. Common Interface and Reload Verification
# 
# The saved interface accepts an exercise name and an optional description. It preserves name-first canonical construction and applies each learned route's saved text preparation exactly once. Identifiers, source labels, and review metadata remain outside model features. Returned scores retain the frozen 16-class order and are identified as uncalibrated probabilities.
# 
# Two fresh Python processes verified the staged release and its final published location using the bundled source modules. Each checked artifact/device reproduced the saved labels for all 435 validation records. Numerical outputs met the fixed tolerances `rtol=1e-5` and `atol=1e-6`, and inference left fitted state unchanged. The neural artifact was checked on both `cuda:0` and the portable CPU application device.
# 
# These repeated validation passes establish loading, serialization, interface consistency, and checked-device reproducibility. They do not add independent exercises or new evidence of classification accuracy. Final held-out classifier evaluation remains Step 32.
# 
# #### 3. Development-Only Catalog Suggestions
# 
# L5 produced one suggestion for each of the 2,434 eligible development records. Training outputs are marked in-sample, and validation outputs are marked development previews.
# 
# | Split | Records | Groups | Source-label agreements | Source-label disagreements | Pending review entries | Actual human decisions |
# |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
# | Training | 1,999 | 1,794 | 1,898 | 101 | 1,999 | 0 |
# | Validation | 435 | 384 | 315 | 120 | 435 | 0 |
# 
# The 221 disagreements are descriptive review candidates. Agreement does not independently verify a source label, and disagreement does not establish that the source is wrong. All 2,434 suggestions remain pending, including those that agree with their source labels. No suggestion was automatically adopted.
# 
# The development catalog retains original label wording, prepared source labels, source-file hashes and row positions, verification status, model identity, canonical input hashes, handling flags, and version-bound suggestion identifiers. Effective labels retain their source origin and recorded pending verification status. The derived export is a development view, not a replacement for the original full source catalog.
# 
# The review workflow requires identifiable, documented decisions before adopting a suggested label. Its authored checks cover review precedence, explicit source rejection, and input/model version binding. Pending worklist entries are not completed human reviews. Existing review evidence and frozen Step 15 benchmark targets remain separate from catalog suggestions.
# 
# #### 4. Protected Populations and Scope
# 
# Whole-group protection excluded all 439 catalog rows in the 385 held-out test groups. This includes 438 eligible test records and one related excluded record. The other 36 excluded records also remained outside prediction and require separate review. Aggregate population accounting covers all 2,909 source catalog rows without exporting protected identifiers or text.
# 
# No test text was transformed or used for prediction. New-record intake was not selected, and complete protected-group screening remains pending. Repeated-relation digests alone do not clear unfamiliar records. Body-part predictions also do not replace basketball skill categories or establish youth suitability, equipment requirements, permission, source accuracy, or planner eligibility.
# 
