model_doc = """# Shared model integration

We use OllamaClient(root, contracts_directory) from src/champion_athletic_map/llm.py.
generate(public_record, instructions, call_id, planner_version=1) uses no reference packet.
Versions 2–4 require reference_packet=packet and share the same public input and packet for a matched case.
Use a stable, unique call ID for each logical request. Completed matching calls reuse their saved result.
Unknown transport outcomes block new submissions; there are no automatic repair generations.
The shared public schema validates inputs. Only the input object enters a model message;
wrapper identifiers and private study annotations stay outside the model context.

The current common policy uses native JSON schema output. All four final-response paths use the same policy.
The original local validator remains authoritative. Raw replies are saved before validation, beside the original input.
The backend renders each complete prompt before generation. Counting includes role formatting and output reserves.
Packet limits alone do not establish complete-request capacity. Step 31 confirms final operating limits.

The current saved response passed format, complete-prompt budget, and factual calendar checks.
The fictional seven-day example preserved both existing practices, including their dates, start/end times and durations,
and added no activities. Earlier failed attempts remain saved. One software example does not establish reliable training planning.
Response types are generated before their dependent fields. Date/time fields are bounded; timing objects include both endpoints,
with null retained for unknown values. Every activity includes its existing-commitment reference array, which may be empty.
Earlier plain-JSON clarification and reference examples remain historical evidence; they do not verify reference-supported
generation under the current schema configuration. Approved resources are active, but automatic rule checking is still pending.
The original emoji-copying failure is also retained. These are development examples, not accepted study cases or benchmark results.
Steps 25–28 develop planner behavior; representative workflow capacity and operational readiness remain pending.
"""
tool_doc = """# Read-only reference tools

ReferenceTools(root, contracts_directory) reads the frozen resources through validated Python methods.
Native model tool calling is not enabled. No lookup refreshes publisher pages or approves source records.

| Method | Arguments | Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| search_references | query, filters=None | Nonblank query; no nonempty filters. Frozen semantic search returns up to five complete reference units with required companions. Ranking alone does not establish answerability. |
| get_drill | drill_id | Approved records return found; held records return not_eligible; aliases resolve to their approved record; unknown IDs return not_found. |
| get_exercise | catalog_id | Known development exercise records return not_eligible; unknown IDs return not_found. No new classification or exercise approval is performed. |
| get_planning_rules | age=None, school_grade=None | Age 13–17 and grade 1–12 when supplied. The active release returns adopted definitions and scope information. Definition availability does not establish compliance or execute rule checks. |
| lookup_food | food_id=None, search_text=None, grams=None, portion_id=None, multiplier=None | Choose ID or description search. Ambiguity requires an exact food selection. Use positive finite grams or a recorded food-specific portion with an explicit multiplier; default is 100 g. |

Results contain request_id, status, data, issues, source_refs and data_version.
Food facts preserve source nutrient IDs, missing values, and recorded zeros; calculations do not prescribe dietary intake.
Whole reference units may be omitted for packet size, with omissions recorded; their required context is not sliced.
Version 1 cannot receive lookup results. Versions 2–4 share the same packet for each matched case.
The original lookup example retains its historical pending statuses. The current approved release is recorded separately.
Gym exercise instructions remain unavailable for planning. Approval does not certify individual athlete suitability or a distinct basketball-drill total.
The saved lookup example and Step 14 calculation evidence remain distinct from future planner evaluations.
"""
