# ### Observation — Step 25
# 
# We tested Llama 3.1:8b on six fictional development profiles from our unified dataset. The planner used the public athlete information and shared instructions without retrieved references or lookup tools. All six model calls completed.
# 
# All replies were valid JSON. Four passed our current validation checks. Two were rejected because some activities incorrectly identified themselves as their own parent activity.
# 
# Manual review also found planning mistakes. One response scheduled three sessions instead of the requested two. Another contained circular activity relationships. The time-conflict example scheduled a session until 18:15 even though availability ended at 17:50. Passing format validation therefore did not guarantee a correct plan.
# 
# The model appropriately asked for the missing participant count and declined the injury-diagnosis request.
# 
# We retained all original responses and failures as our baseline. These findings cover six development examples; formal plan-quality and rule-compliance scores remain pending.

# <hr style="border: none; height: 10px; background-color: #FFD700;">

