# ### Step 31-2 — Review the pilot cases and weekly schedule checks
# 
# Before running the four planners, we will check whether our selected examples
# test what we intended. We will review the request, available time, equipment,
# practice space and existing commitments. We will keep a separate record of the
# expected behaviour, possible activities and any unresolved questions. These
# review notes will stay outside the information given to the model.
# 
# Our original profiles did not explicitly say whether their existing commitments
# covered the whole week. Without that statement, an apparently free day could
# still contain unreported training. We will create a new version of the fictional
# pilot profiles with a clear weekly schedule-coverage field. For nineteen cases,
# we will explicitly write that the listed commitments cover all existing training
# and sport activity, including informal sessions. This is new information authored
# for our fictional examples; an empty list by itself does not establish completeness.
# The example with an unknown existing schedule will retain that missing information.
# We will preserve every earlier field and keep the original profiles and results.
# 
# We will also test a separate version of the schedule checker. It will confirm
# weekly limits and rest days only when the reported coverage matches the planning
# week and the calendar, activity relationships and timing are complete and valid.
# For these pass checks, every calendar session will count as potentially relevant
# training, including existing commitments. This conservative bound prevents an
# activity from escaping the calculation because of its name.
# Known violations will remain violations. The existing advisory guidance will
# retain its original meaning.
# 
# This review does not make every proposed exercise feasible. Some examples still
# need clearer evidence about partner positions, space or the time needed for a
# source activity. We will retain those conditions and keep full resource checking
# and independent scoring pending. We will record this as an assistant review under
# Sam's delegated authority; it does not claim a second human review or acceptance
# of the final study cases.
# 
# The cell below will check and save this preparation. It will make no model or
# reference-encoding calls. All four planners must receive the same versioned public
# facts when we run the next operational test. The full pilot and final protocol
# will remain unfinished until their remaining requirements are met.
# 

# In[6]:


