# activities too generally to verify their resource requirements. We will keep
# those findings and use them to make the shared task instructions clearer.
# 
# We will now apply the same clarification to all four planner versions. It will
# ask each planner to follow the requested number of additional sessions rather
# than filling every available slot, describe the actual activities and setup,
# and explicitly address any supplied food question. Unknown information must
# remain unknown. The guidance will not supply an activity choice, a food answer
# or private assessment results.
# 
# We will test a different fictional development athlete: a 15-year-old beginner
# working on shooting consistency. The request asks for two additional practices
# although three time slots are available and the maximum is three. It also
# includes an existing soccer practice and a question about the recorded protein
# in 150 g of Medjool dates. We will use the already versioned public information
# without changing it. This gives us a fresh example of the same request-handling
# problem before we run the larger pilot.
# 
