# Planner 1 will still work from the public request alone. Planners 2–4 will use
# their normal reference access, with matching complete reference packets. We will
# keep the prepared planner order, original checks and revision limits. Planner 4
# will use the lossless review encoding we already tested, so complete findings
# take less space without removing information. Every complete request must still
# fit the existing prompt budget before generation.
# 
# The cell will run this one matched four-planner test and then apply the saved
# independent checks to each designated reply. It will check the session count,
# calendar, food answer and resource evidence separately from Planner 4's internal
# review. Resource descriptions outside our limited reviewed coverage will remain
# unverified. A correct format or an internal approval will not be treated as a
# successful plan by itself.
# 
# We will save this as a new development experiment. Earlier prompts, results and
# failed replies will remain in place. Completed matching jobs will be reused if
# we rerun this cell; weak answers will not automatically trigger another attempt.
# An uncertain model request will stop the run for review. This small test does
# not complete the full pilot, establish a planner ranking or produce final study
