# ### Step 31-7 — Strengthen the response requirements
# 
# Our saved replies show that the food information reached the reference-supported
# planners, but none included the requested answer. In the specialist workflows,
# the food role returned empty content while marking its contribution as provided.
# Our note schema accepted that empty contribution, and the final response schema
# allowed the food answer to be omitted. We will correct these gaps in the response
# requirements before spending more time on generation.
# 
# When the public input contains a food question, all four planner versions will
# now be required to include a food statement near the beginning of the response.
# The statement can give the supported answer or explain that the information is
# unavailable. Planner 1 will still receive no lookup values or references. The
# food specialist must provide a nonempty recommendation, or use an unavailable
# status with an explanation. A longer rationale alone will not count as content.
# These changes require an explicit response; they cannot guarantee that the
# response is relevant or numerically correct.
# 
# We will also derive the planning window and allowed dates from the public input.
# Local validation will check the exact seven dates in chronological order. The
# native generation schema will restrict the allowed dates, while ordering and
# duplicate-date checks will remain in local validation. Session counts, existing
# practices, activity relationships and resource requirements will keep their
# independent checks. We will not fill in or repair a generated plan after the fact.
