# The prospective runtime will apply the same final response contract to all four
# planners and Planner 4's revisions. It will use the stronger food-note contract
# only for the food role, with the same schema used for generation and parsing.
# We will clarify the existing instruction about omitting irrelevant fields so a
# requested food answer cannot be treated as optional. The same model, token
# reserves, revision limits and required checks will stay in place.
# 
# This cell will test the new requirements and check them against the saved
# replies. It will make no model calls, run no reference search, and leave the
# earlier results unchanged. Rejecting a known bad reply shows that the contract
# catches that error; it does not prove better future generation. The new native
# schema still needs a separate backend compatibility check and a bounded model
# test before we can claim an improvement. The full pilot and final scoring remain
# pending.
