# ### Step 31-9 — Correct the operational failures and retain the model findings
# 
# The saved live test shows why two workflows did not finish. Planner 1 spent its
# entire reply allowance generating a long, invented source URL. Planner 4's first
# revision prompt exceeded its input allowance by 207 tokens. These failures need
# specific operational changes. Increasing the reply allowance would only give
# the URL loop more room, and changing the context size is unnecessary for the
# saved revision if we remove repeated metadata without removing information.
# 
# We will limit food identifiers and source URLs to reasonable lengths, while
# keeping null values available when a source is unknown. The same limits will
# apply to all four planners. This prevents an unbounded URL in those fields; it
# does not make a generated citation correct.
# 
# We will also store repeated nutrition-reference fields once in the model input
# and keep each nutrient's differing values in its own row. The complete original
# data must be recovered exactly, including types, missing values and source
# qualifications. This representation will apply consistently to the workflows
# that receive references. Planner 1 will continue to receive no reference data.
# Our saved-request replay places the blocked revision within the current budget,
# but every future live request will still need its normal backend-rendered check.
# 
# The other two planners returned valid JSON and the requested number of extra
# sessions, but they omitted both existing practices and copied the food question
# instead of answering it. We will retain those as model findings. Our independent
# food check will recognize an exact question echo as a missing answer, rather
# than treating the question's quantity as a possible nutrient claim. A truthful
# unknown will remain unverified, and no source value will be inserted into the
# model's reply by our code.
# 
# This cell will test the operational changes, review the saved results and save
# a new runtime and assessment candidate. It will make no new model calls and
# will leave earlier results in place. These changes do not guarantee a complete
# calendar or correct food answer. We will use one recorded configuration for the
# remaining development pilot and report failures and unknowns, rather than keep
# regenerating these examples until they pass. Final scoring and the full study
# protocol remain separate work.
# 

