preparation.__spec__.loader.exec_module(preparation)
summary = preparation.prepare(root, software_evidence=software_evidence)
preparation.print_summary(summary)


# ### Step 31-10 — Run the development pilot in small batches
# 
# We have finished the targeted operational corrections. We will now run the
# twenty development cases we selected earlier through all four planner versions,
# using one recorded configuration. This gives us eighty planner outcomes across
# ages 13–17, including planning requests, missing information, conflicting
# constraints and requests outside our scope. These cases remain provisional
# development examples; they are not the final accepted study population.
# Some have already appeared in our earlier checks, so this run measures the
# development configuration rather than performance on unseen final cases.
# 
# We will use the same model and generation settings for the four versions.
# Planner 1 will continue without reference access. The other versions will use
# matching complete reference packets, with repeated nutrition metadata encoded
# without removing information. The updated field limits and independent food
# checks will apply as prepared. We will keep the original case order and the
# balanced planner order within each case.
# 
# We will retain every designated result. A valid format will not be treated as a
# correct plan by itself. Missing practices, incorrect food answers, inappropriate
# responses, execution failures and unresolved resource checks will stay in the
# records. Planner 4's internal approval will not replace the independent checks,
# and an earlier draft will not replace a failed final workflow. We will not
# regenerate completed jobs to search for better replies.
# 
# The cell will start up to five cases each time we run it. It will save results
# after each planner job and check the four outcomes for each completed case.
# When the batch finishes, running this same cell again will continue with the
# next cases. Previously completed cases will be verified and skipped. Four full
# five-case batches cover all twenty cases; no additional numbered code cells are
# needed for those batches.
# 
# Each batch may take several minutes, especially when references load or Planner
# 4 uses its revision allowance. We will wait for the cell to finish before
# starting the next batch. An uncertain model request, incomplete reference
# preparation or changed dependency will stop progress for review. A recorded
# model failure still belongs in the results and does not trigger a retry.
# 
# This step measures the development workflows. It does not create final study
# scores, establish a winning planner or complete the human review. We will use
# the full set of saved outcomes to finish the remaining scoring preparation and
# document the model and checker limitations.
# 

