# ### Step 31-13 — Correct the reference workflow and check it offline
# 
# Our saved-reply review showed a gap between having approved basketball drills
# in our data and actually supplying them to the planners. We will correct that
# connection before making another model request. The new selector will rank
# approved variants using the athlete's stated goals and resources, fetch the
# complete records, and include a relevant variant when one fits the context.
# It will retain the source conditions and record unavailable or unresolved
# requirements. Selecting a reference will not certify that an athlete can
# perform it or that a whole plan is feasible.
# 
# We will also make the requested food fact easier to find. The reference-based
# planners will receive a compact view of the food, amount, nutrient, recorded
# value and source, alongside the complete lookup data. They will still write
# their own answers. Planner 1 will continue without reference access and may
# honestly state that a fact is unknown. We will retain the same model, context
# limit and output allowances.
# 
# The corrected checking layer will recognize copied food questions with changed
# quotation marks, require evidence for conflict explanations, separate activity
# link errors from proven time-limit overruns, and keep existing-event resources
# separate from resources for extra sessions. It will continue to record unknown
# evidence and enforce the remaining required checks. Earlier responses and
# their original assessments will stay unchanged.
# 
# We will save this as a new development candidate. This cell installs the new
# modules, runs offline checks, and uses the saved public rankings to check
# reference selection and packet capacity. It does not generate new responses
# or run the query encoder. The original packets remain available, and the new
# diagnostic packets will not be substituted for fresh, matched inputs in a live
# test. Complete-request backend checks and a small balanced model test will
# still be needed before we can assess the revised workflow's results.
# 

