# ### Step 31-17 — Review our saved results and record the remaining limitations
# 
# We have completed the development pilot, a smaller test of the corrected
# workflow, and one continuation of a saved Planner 4 draft. The continuation
# confirmed that the corrected requests could pass the backend rendering and
# budget checks. Its final reply also used a valid response format and included
# the requested two additional sessions. However, it omitted both existing
# practices, left out the new sessions' start and end times, and repeated the food
# question instead of answering it. These findings keep the plan from passing
# our required checks.
# 
# We will now bring the saved results together in a report. We will keep three
# sections: the original twenty-case pilot, the four repeated cases tested after
# workflow corrections, and the single Planner 4 continuation. We will show
# format validity, response completion and the number of plan-type replies
# passing all their recorded required checks. We will retain the assessments
# made under each saved workflow version. The four repeated cases and the
# continuation are development follow-ups; we will keep the original pilot's
# case count unchanged. Our earlier review also found that the original pilot
# did not deliver the approved drill context. We will retain that limitation
# when discussing what its reference-assisted results show.
# 
# We will distinguish demonstrated errors from missing evidence. Omitting a
# supplied practice or copying a question is a visible failure. An unverified
# resource finding can also reflect the limits of our checker's supported
# wording. The drill records remain approved; approval alone does not establish
# that a generated session follows their actions, setup and participant roles.
# We will leave those uncertainties visible instead of turning them into passes
# or treating them as proven equipment shortages.
# 
# This cell will read the saved replies and assessments, check that each
# assessment still matches its reply, and save a separate summary and written review. It will
# make no model requests or reference searches and will preserve the previous
# results. Our conclusion will describe what these development tests support;
# it will not assign a winning planner, create human ratings, or claim final
# study scores or operational readiness. Human review and final scoring remain
# the next evaluation tasks.
# 

