# ### Step 33-1 — Prepare the final-case review package
# 
# We will begin by making the saved candidate cases easier to review. The package will contain readable case cards, the original public inputs, private annotation and feasibility worksheets, and editable review files. It will also identify our current approved basketball resources and planning rules so that reviewers can assess the cases against the resources the planners will actually use.
# 
# For each case, we need to establish the appropriate response, the important conditions to check and its relationship to other cases. For a case described as feasible, we also need a reviewed example showing that the request can be fulfilled with the approved resources and stated constraints. That example is evidence that a solution exists; it is not the only acceptable answer.
# 
# Our saved case-review requirements call for a preparer and a different teammate to review these decisions. We will leave their names and decisions blank until those reviews take place. This preparation review is separate from Step 34, where teammates will rate the generated responses.
# 
# The current input format includes explicit statements about schedule completeness. Any proposed change from the older case format will remain a proposal until reviewed. An empty list of commitments will not automatically mean that the athlete has no other commitments.
# 
# We will carry forward the reference-search assessment already completed in Step 23. Its results cover a limited collection of 11 reference units and will be reported separately from planner quality. The original retrieval results and development pilot responses will remain preserved.
# 
# Private categories, expected answers, family decisions and feasibility examples belong to the evaluation materials. They must stay outside planner prompts, reference-search documents and Version 4's internal evaluator. The application will continue using the L5 classifier selected during validation; Step 32's test findings will not change the planner inputs.
# 
# The cell will prepare the review package and save a short summary. Final planner generation, independent scoring and the anonymized response-review package will follow after the final cases and operating settings are accepted and frozen.
# 

